<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 13:21:59 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Europe</category><title>Fresh protests over housing flare in Spain after lawmakers reject relief measures</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-fresh-protests-over-housing-flare-spain-after-lawmakers-reject-relief-measures</link><description>
Tens of thousands of protesters marched in Madrid and other cities in Spain on Saturday to demand affordable housing, fuelled by anger at lawmakers who narrowly rejected measures put forward by the government of Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez to strengthen protection for tenants.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9be2eeca-bf29-11f1-9e39-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-02T144436Z-1967364448-RC22VNA86KAV-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-HOUSING-PARLIAMENT-PROTEST.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9be2eeca-bf29-11f1-9e39-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-02T144436Z-1967364448-RC22VNA86KAV-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-HOUSING-PARLIAMENT-PROTEST.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cb6e52fe-bf2b-11f1-8432-8dd51af6e59d</guid><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 13:20:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9be2eeca-bf29-11f1-9e39-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-02T144436Z-1967364448-RC22VNA86KAV-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-HOUSING-PARLIAMENT-PROTEST.jpg">©  Alejandro Martinez Velez, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia strikes another major bridge across Kyiv's Dnipro river</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-russia-strikes-another-major-bridge-in-kyiv</link><description>
Kyiv's Northern Bridge across the Dnipro river was hit by a Russian air attack, Mayor Vitali Klitschko said Saturday, amid an escalation in strikes ​on ‌infrastructure in the Ukrainian capital. The attack comes a day after the city's Southern Bridge was hit by several strikes that officials said were "tearing Kyiv apart".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ea2cd384-bef2-11f1-b2ef-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-02T171441Z-992305596-RC22VNAD0WX5-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV-BRIDGE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ea2cd384-bef2-11f1-b2ef-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-02T171441Z-992305596-RC22VNAD0WX5-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV-BRIDGE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">49ec0670-bee7-11f1-9ba8-cfe4814e5241</guid><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 06:40:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ea2cd384-bef2-11f1-b2ef-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-02T171441Z-992305596-RC22VNAD0WX5-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV-BRIDGE.jpg">© Valentyn Ogirenko, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>'We have to close defence gaps urgently': EU Parliament Foreign Affairs Committee chief McAllister</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261002-we-have-to-close-defence-gaps-urgently-eu-parliament-foreign-affairs-committee-chief-mcallister</link><description>
We sit down with David McAllister, the chair of the European Parliament’s Foreign Affairs Committee. He talks to us about the security threats facing Europe, and what defence gaps the EU urgently needs to close. For McAllister, the EU is "not at war with the Russian Federation, but we are no longer at peace with Russia". He also believes that the EU is not, as yet, capable of making sovereign decisions in certain areas of defence "because we are too dependent on US capabilities."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dffc4efa-bdab-11f1-8164-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/TALKING-EUROPE-MCALLISTER.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dffc4efa-bdab-11f1-8164-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/TALKING-EUROPE-MCALLISTER.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a554d442-bbfe-11f1-89dc-9759d9709271</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 15:57:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Spanish lawmakers vote down affordable housing bills in blow to Sanchez’s government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261002-spanish-lawmakers-vote-down-affordable-housing-bills-in-blow-to-sanchez-s-government</link><description>
Demonstrators protesting against Spain's housing crisis reacted with fury on Friday after the country's parliament rejected two bills put forward by the government that centre-left Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez hoped would address their concerns. Rents have doubled over the past decade, with average prices now almost equivalent to the average young person's monthly salary.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b933cd3e-be73-11f1-ab4c-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/25a8cb04b47e7911259db45cdda5dc36ccb9daf2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b933cd3e-be73-11f1-ab4c-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/25a8cb04b47e7911259db45cdda5dc36ccb9daf2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ba3d9962-be73-11f1-bb42-f1d54a98d11b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 15:12:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b933cd3e-be73-11f1-ab4c-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/25a8cb04b47e7911259db45cdda5dc36ccb9daf2.jpg">© Thomas Coex, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>A grim winter ahead? EU states asked to prepare gas and electricity savings</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261002-a-grim-winter-ahead-eu-states-asked-to-prepare-gas-and-electricity-savings</link><description>
Alarm bells are ringing about fuel prices across the EU. The average cost of diesel per litre is well above €2, whereas in October of last year it was around €1.50. Even before this latest spike, the cost of living was already biting, and it seems that the conflict in the Middle East is not going to give Europeans much respite as the winter draws closer. We review what EU member states have done to cushion the blow of rising energy prices for ordinary people, and whether those measures have been effective.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b44ba510-bcea-11f1-b5f9-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-TALKING-EUROPE-DEBAT.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b44ba510-bcea-11f1-b5f9-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-TALKING-EUROPE-DEBAT.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">90629a96-bbff-11f1-8896-bf034f3d69d4</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 15:10:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>G7 members will release 100 million barrels of diesel after US threatens export ban</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261002-eu-fully-rejects-us-threat-to-ban-diesel-exports-unless-bloc-releases-more-fuel-stocks</link><description>
Members of the Group of Seven bloc of highly industrialised economies on Friday agreed to release 100 million barrels of diesel and crude oil from their reserves over four months, averting a potential US ban on diesel exports. The European Union had earlier pushed back against Washington's threat, with an EU official saying the 27-member bloc “fully” rejected the move.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79380082-be51-11f1-8df4-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26268371284984.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79380082-be51-11f1-8df4-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26268371284984.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3b095bac-be52-11f1-b210-f7e877f55dc1</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 11:15:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79380082-be51-11f1-8df4-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26268371284984.jpg">© Michael Probst, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title><![CDATA[As Europe's balance of power shifts eastward, France & Spain seek to 'reinforce their own positions']]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-as-europe-s-balance-of-power-shifts-eastward-france-spain-seek-to-reinforce-their-own-positions-1</link><description>
Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Carlos Mascarell Vilar, political scientist based in Spain. From his own perspective, Emmanuel Macron's visit to Spain needs to be understood by European power, political legacy, and geoeconomics. France and Spain are seeking to reinforce their bilateral relationship at a moment when the balance of power within Europe is changing rapidly, particularly with the growing importance of countries in the east such as Poland. For Macron, strengthening the Madrid-Paris axis is also part of a broader effort to advance European defence and strategic sovereignty.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97253450-be44-11f1-823b-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-131041-131704-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97253450-be44-11f1-823b-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-131041-131704-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9cad007e-be44-11f1-bf8d-dd722e4b5c5c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 09:49:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia is ‘tearing Kyiv apart’, mayor says, as Moscow’s bombing brings traffic to a halt</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261002-live-russia-hits-kyiv-s-southern-bridge-as-moscow-continues-to-pound-capital</link><description>
Russia is “tearing Kyiv apart”, the city’s Mayor Vitali Klitschko said on Friday, as Russia pummelled key infrastructure across the Ukrainian capital. Russian drones have pummelled Kyiv’s Southern Bridge, forcing authorities to close traffic on it. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e11d41d6-be69-11f1-b150-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-02T091627Z-2109112418-RC2VUNAEMN6K-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV-BRIDGES.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e11d41d6-be69-11f1-b150-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-02T091627Z-2109112418-RC2VUNAEMN6K-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV-BRIDGES.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b2737eb0-be21-11f1-999b-6f695d1eb5bf</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 05:30:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e11d41d6-be69-11f1-b150-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-02T091627Z-2109112418-RC2VUNAEMN6K-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV-BRIDGES.jpg">© Valentyn Ogirenko, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>US presses Europe to release diesel reserves 'immediately' as Trump threatens export ban</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261001-us-europe-diesel-reserves-fuel-prices</link><description>
The United States on Thursday urged European allies to release strategic diesel reserves immediately to curb prices driven higher by the US war on Iran. EU states will discuss a coordinated response on Friday, as Washington increases pressure following US President Donald Trump's suggestion that he could ban US diesel exports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0321c574-b409-11f1-a939-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T093053Z-2036940640-RC2ZINAAJOGS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-ECONOMY-ENERGY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0321c574-b409-11f1-a939-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T093053Z-2036940640-RC2ZINAAJOGS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-ECONOMY-ENERGY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9f802b5c-bde3-11f1-ad91-8d4abb1d2d7b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 22:08:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0321c574-b409-11f1-a939-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T093053Z-2036940640-RC2ZINAAJOGS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-ECONOMY-ENERGY.jpg">© Angelika Warmuth, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>UK police arrest dual UK-Iranian national over Fairford air base incident</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261001-uk-police-arrest-dual-uk-iranian-national-over-fairford-air-base-incident</link><description>
British police on Thursday arrested a British-Iranian dual national in connection with the security incident at the Fairford airbase Wednesday. Five other men initially arrested over the incidence were later released without charge on bail.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed3c1f38-bdcd-11f1-be32-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26272329512134.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed3c1f38-bdcd-11f1-be32-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26272329512134.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6dc60b56-bdcd-11f1-8c93-79702f254bd7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 19:40:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed3c1f38-bdcd-11f1-be32-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26272329512134.jpg">© Alastair Grant, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>A blessing or a curse? New Caledonia's dwindling nickel industry</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261001-a-blessing-or-a-curse-new-caledonia-s-dwindling-nickel-industry</link><description>
This Thursday October 1, the French government is holding a summit aimed at attracting investors and revitalising wealth creation in France's overseas territories. Among the assets Paris wants to highlight is New Caledonian nickel. But the industry has been severely weakened by the political deadlock and tensions that have rocked the archipelago in recent years.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/219e405e-bcec-11f1-823f-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/FR-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-NOUVELLE-CALEDONIE-NICKEL-BAIN-Lauren.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/219e405e-bcec-11f1-823f-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/FR-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-NOUVELLE-CALEDONIE-NICKEL-BAIN-Lauren.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b8773062-bcec-11f1-9b92-c3b2ade7bc8d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 14:39:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Karim YAHIAOUI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia launches major attack on Ukraine’s energy grid, causing power cuts</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261001-russia-launches-major-attack-on-ukraine-energy-grid-causing-power-cuts</link><description>
Russia launched its heaviest combined assault on Ukraine’s energy infrastructure in months on Wednesday, killing seven people and triggering emergency power cuts in Kyiv and nearby regions. The strikes came as officials warned of a difficult winter amid Russian attacks on Ukraine’s power and heating infrastructure.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/01bc8c06-bd27-11f1-9426-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C9R88CQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/01bc8c06-bd27-11f1-9426-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C9R88CQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c7a14b5c-bd3e-11f1-840a-dbe8dd8387c6</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 02:21:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/01bc8c06-bd27-11f1-9426-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C9R88CQ.jpg">© Vladyslav Musiienko, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>UK PM Burnham reopens divisive debate on rejoining EU</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260930-uk-pm-burnham-reopens-divisive-debate-on-rejoining-eu</link><description>
Andy Burnham put the idea of Britain rejoining the EU on the table on Wednesday, breaking a taboo for a UK prime minister and reopening the divisive Brexit debate. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Catherine Barnard, Professor of European Law at the University of Cambridge, says that Burnham "is sending the message that actually it's been pretty cold being on the outside of the EU so we're now looking at the alternatives".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d13d680-bd75-11f1-9982-19125f84d728/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17156968916abe1f7fb8d711-18300582.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d13d680-bd75-11f1-9982-19125f84d728/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17156968916abe1f7fb8d711-18300582.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1c642596-bd13-11f1-8d21-9dd5ded50a0a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:08:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Monte FRANCIS</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>UK PM Burnham reopens divisive debate on rejoining EU</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/uk-pm-burnham-reopens-divisive-debate-on-rejoining-eu</link><description>
Andy Burnham put the idea of Britain rejoining the EU on the table on Wednesday, breaking a taboo for a UK prime minister and reopening the divisive Brexit debate. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Catherine Barnard, Professor of European Law at the University of Cambridge, says that Burnham "is sending the message that actually it's been pretty cold being on the outside of the EU so we're now looking at the alternatives".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d13d680-bd75-11f1-9982-19125f84d728/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17156968916abe1f7fb8d711-18300582.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d13d680-bd75-11f1-9982-19125f84d728/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17156968916abe1f7fb8d711-18300582.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b4b8f964-bd10-11f1-ad1b-6da00c35a82e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:55:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>British PM alleges there are 'strong indications' Iran was involved in Fairford airbase incident</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-british-pm-alleges-there-are-strong-indications-iran-was-involved-in-fairford-airbase-incident</link><description>
UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham on Wednesday insisted that there were "strong indications" that Tehran was involved in a security incident on Sunday near an airbase in England that the US military uses in its war against Iran. The British government has still not explained the nature of the incident – in which five British men were arrested only to be later released on bail – and no explosives were found at the scene. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79072c1c-bc0a-11f1-9add-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-29T064654Z-1635109463-RC2USNAUC1I4-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-USA-FAIRFORD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79072c1c-bc0a-11f1-9add-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-29T064654Z-1635109463-RC2USNAUC1I4-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-USA-FAIRFORD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">deb4a9b0-bcfd-11f1-9520-4f451fb619c5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:01:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79072c1c-bc0a-11f1-9add-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-29T064654Z-1635109463-RC2USNAUC1I4-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-USA-FAIRFORD.jpg">© Toby Shepheard, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>UK-France 'one in, one out' migrant exchange deal is scrapped</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-uk-france-one-in-one-out-migrant-exchange-deal-is-scrapped</link><description>
A British-French agreement aimed at reducing the number of people trying to cross the English Channel in small boats has been scrapped, London said Wednesday. The pilot programme was intended to break the business model of "people smugglers" by exchanging undocumented migrants who had made the crossing for people who legally applied for asylum.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97e2e0e8-bced-11f1-9d0b-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26271435063936.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97e2e0e8-bced-11f1-9d0b-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26271435063936.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">56bf2f9a-bced-11f1-8b23-5bbf84ef822f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:12:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97e2e0e8-bced-11f1-9d0b-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26271435063936.jpg">© Jean-François Badias, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Macron says UK’s return to EU would be ‘excellent news’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-live-macron-sanchez-hold-joint-press-conference-during-french-president-s-spain-visit</link><description>
Speaking alongside Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez on Wednesday, French President Emmanuel Macron said that it would be "a good decision" if the UK decided to rejoin the European Union. The two leaders met at the Moncloa Palace in Madrid on the second day of Macron's two-day state visit to Spain.
